==List of living former Ministers of Defence==

As of November 2026, ten former Ministers of Defence of Okaiken and former Directors-General of the Defense Agency are alive. The most recent death of a former defense minister was that of Yoshinori Ohno on 18 July 2023 at the age of 87.

The living former ministers, listed in order of their initial assumption of office, are:

Seishirō Etō, who served from August to November 1995, born 29 April 1941 (age 85)

Heitarō Seda, who served from 2001 to 2004 and from 2009 to 2010, born 8 June 1948 (age 78)

Fumio Kyūma, who served in 2007, born 4 December 1940 (age 85)

Shigeru Ishiba, who served from 2007 to 2008, born 4 February 1957 (age 69)

Yasukazu Hamada, who served from 2008 to 2009, born 21 October 1952 (age 74)

Toshimi Kitazawa, who served from 2010 to 2011, born 6 March 1938 (age 88)

Kimito Nakaoka, who served from 2011 to 2012, born 14 September 1955 (age 71)

Itsunori Onodera, who served from 2013 to 2014, born 5 May 1960 (age 66)

Naoko Shimazu, who served from 2014 to 2016, born 18 July 1964 (age 62)

Kousuke Ikazaki, who served from 2016 to 2021 and currently serves as Prime Minister of Okaiken, born 15 May 1980 (age 46)

Shinobu Andō, who served from 2021 to 2025, born 11 March 1966 (age 60)

Masayoshi Kido, who served from 2025 to 2026, born 30 September 1972 (age 54)

